  "Carnegie granted Anacortes $10,000 on December 14, 1908. Wikipedia's list names the designers as Cox, Piper and Carder of Bellingham; the state's 1982 survey of Washington's Carnegie libraries gives the firm as Piper and Cox. By 1981 it had become a museum, and it is the Anacortes Museum now. On the National Register.",
