  "Carnegie granted $10,000 on December 13, 1909. Wikipedia's list says Wilson and Ginnold drew it in a Spanish Revival style and R. L. Ross built it; the 1982 state survey says sources disagree on whether it was Harold Ginnold or C. Lewis Wilson. By 1981 it was a museum, and it is now the Franklin County Historical Museum. On the National Register since 1982.",
